  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A voice powerful beyond anything Flood Extremity can imagine suppresses him completely inside the fate reversing refinement sub formation, telling him not to be afraid and not to move. The voice calls him the descendant of its master and promises not to eat him as long as he does not attack. A huge, purple-furred, dog-tailed beast then reveals itself, rejects being called a steed, and gives its own name: Mao Li Qiu, or Grandpa Mao for short. Grandpa Mao slashes apart the sub formation Black Extremity had built with much difficulty, binds Flood Extremity and Black Extremity in its breath, and carries them flying toward Reverse Flow River to retrieve Ma Hong Yun and the love Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        1278
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_flood_extremity",
        "char_sun_ming_lu",
        "loc_reverse_flow_river",
        "char_ma_hong_yun",
        "gu_love_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Old Ancestor Xue Hu is surprised when the dog tail life extending ferret Mao Li Qiu appears instead of staying in its cave. Narration states it was Giant Sun Immortal Venerable’s steed, subdued in Giant Sun’s later years for lifespan methods, enlightened to intelligence, and able to use Gu worms and immortal killer moves. Black Extremity calls it Grandpa Mao while they watch Reverse Flow River.",
      "chapters": [
        1280
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "watching-reverse-flow-river",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_old_ancestor_xue_hu",
        "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable",
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "It is grouped with Di Zang Sheng and Huo Kong as unique immemorial desolate beasts at the peak of rank eight battle strength.",
      "chapters": [
        1280
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "watching-reverse-flow-river",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_di_zang_sheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "It is hill-like in size and its eyes shine a purple crystal color.",
      "chapters": [
        1278
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its beast face makes very human-like expressions.",
      "chapters": [
        1280
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "It bares sharp fangs and its hair stands on end when it is agitated.",
      "chapters": [
        1284
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "It scratches deep marks into the ground with its claws.",
      "chapters": [
        1285
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "As it ages the dog tail shrinks with its lifespan and vanishes near death. When it senses the end it can devour an immemorial desolate beast dog, gain that lifespan, and grow the tail again, which is why it still lives after Giant Sun’s death.",
      "chapters": [
        1280
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan escapes the chaotic battle at Reverse Flow River, but Mao Li Qiu refuses to stop chasing him, and Fang Yuan is not its match. Once he crosses into the regional wall it can only watch, since it was born a wild beast of Northern Plains and the wall restricts it.",
      "chapters": [
        1289
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "escape-by-the-regional-wall",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "reg_northern_plains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later recalls escaping the ferret by way of the regional wall.",
      "chapters": [
        1361
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "escape-by-the-regional-wall",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When a Heavenly Court and ten great ancient sects group is crushed trying to save Ma Hong Yun in Northern Plains, two of its three rank eight Gu Immortals die and one goes missing, and Mao Li Qiu is named as the one who killed them.",
      "chapters": [
        1334
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "heavenly-courts-rank-eights-fall",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    }
  ],
